FlexCAN_T4 — Complete Reference Guide
Repository: github.com/tonton81/FlexCAN_T4 Author: Antonio Alexander Brewer (tonton81) · License: MIT Platforms: Teensy 3.2/3.5/3.6 (Kinetis) and Teensy 4.0/4.1 (i.MX RT1062)

FlexCAN_T4 is a from-the-ground-up rewrite of the older "IFCT" library for driving the FlexCAN peripherals built into PJRC's Teensy boards. It supports classic CAN 2.0 frames everywhere, and CAN FD (flexible data rate, up to 64-byte payloads) on the Teensy 4's third CAN controller. The library is entirely interrupt/queue driven under the hood, but exposes both a simple polling API and a callback-based API, so it can be used however fits your sketch.

This guide is organized as a practical walkthrough followed by a full API reference, based on the library's README.md and its public header (FlexCAN_T4.h).

